course: dictionary
lesson: 8979
title: Sir, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word sir has more than one meaning, so context matters. Look at who is speaking, who is spoken to, and where it happens. In a shop, «Can I help you, sir?» means a polite way to speak to a man whose name you do not know.
explain: In a classroom in Britain, a pupil may say «Yes, sir» to a male teacher. The clues are the school setting and the teacher. Sir means the male teacher here, not a shopkeeper.
explain: With a capital S, Sir is a title for a knight, as in «Sir Isaac Newton». A name follows it. Check by swapping in your meaning: does «polite way to speak to a man» fit the sentence, or does «title for a knight» fit better?
fact: Sir is a polite word for a man whose name you do not know, or a man in charge.
fact: In the UK and Ireland, pupils often call a male teacher «sir».
fact: Capital Sir is a title for a knight, as in «Sir Isaac Newton».
fact: Sir has a plural, sirs, and phrases such as «yes sir», «no sir» and «Dear Sir».
fact: In shops and restaurants, staff may say «sir» to be polite.
exercise: «Why, certainly, sir … our shops keep open to all sorts of hours.» What does sir mean here? | *A polite way to speak to a man whose name the speaker does not know | A title for a knight | The name of a shop | A teacher in a classroom
exercise: A pupil says «Sorry, sir, you were right» to a male teacher. Who is sir? | A shopkeeper speaking to a customer | *The male teacher | Sir Isaac Newton | A knight in a castle
exercise: Which example shows Sir as a knight's title? | Dear Sir | *Sir Isaac Newton | Sirs | Yes, sir
test: The Rat tells him «You needn't sir me quite so much». What is the Rat asking him to do? | Call him Sir Rat | *Be less formal and polite | Whisper softly | Say sir more often
test: Pupils in Britain call a female teacher «Miss». What do they call a male teacher? | *Sir | Miss | Knight | Dear
exam: What does sir mean in «Can I help you, sir?» | A title for a knight | The name of a shop | *A polite way to speak to a man whose name you do not know | A teacher in a school
